__d(function(g,r,i,a,m,e,d){"use strict";Object.defineProperty(e,'__esModule',{value:!0}),Object.defineProperty(e,"HELP",{enumerable:!0,get:function(){return t}}),r(d[0]);const t=[{id:'premium',question:'What is FIG Premium?',topic:'Pricing',forBusiness:!0,intro:'An optional $50 a year for your whole account, every location included. Everything else on FIG stays free.',boxTitle:'What Premium adds',bullets:['Unlimited locations (free accounts have up to 2).','Deal announcements: every 2 hours, a short note to every diner in your restaurant\u2019s area (Markham diners for a Markham restaurant), and to everyone who saved you. Diners can turn these off.','Area insights: when diners near you claim deals, what they crave, trends, and the restaurants and deals around you.','Menu from a photo: snap your menu or paste its link, and FIG types up every dish and price.','A FIG Premium badge on your restaurant page. It never moves you up in search or on the map.'],outro:'Find it in Settings \u2192 FIG Premium. It renews every year, and you can cancel anytime there.'},{id:'cost',question:'What does FIG cost?',topic:'Pricing',forBusiness:!0,intro:'FIG is free for restaurants. Signing up, setting up your page, going live, posting deals, scanning and the dashboard cost nothing, and there\u2019s no commission on the bill. FIG only earns a small share of takeout orders paid in the app.',boxTitle:'What you pay',bullets:['Dine-in deals and scans: no fee per scan or per diner.','Takeout orders paid in the app: FIG keeps 5% of the food before tax, and Stripe\u2019s card fee comes off the same payment. The rest, tax included, is paid out to you.'],outro:'No contract, and nothing to cancel. Insights, in Settings, show what your deals bring in.'},{id:'biz-setup',question:'How do I set up my page?',topic:'Setting up',forBusiness:!0,intro:'Open Home and follow Get FIG ready. The rows tick themselves as you go: your page, your menu, your first deal, connecting Stripe to publish, a look at your page as a diner sees it, your team, and takeout if you want it.',boxTitle:'What goes on your page',bullets:['Photos: 1 to 8. Three or more looks best.','Your cuisine, price range, phone number and opening hours.','Your menu, in sections with prices. Take a photo of it, or paste its link, and FIG types it up for you. You check every line before diners see it. You can also type it in.','Deals, when you are ready.'],outro:'Setting up is free, and you can build all of it before you connect Stripe. Until you do, your page, menu and deals are drafts that only your team can see. Connect Stripe to publish them. Diners open on January 1, 2027, so a published page says Ready until then, and nothing is lost by getting it right first.'},{id:'biz-stripe',question:'Why do I connect Stripe?',topic:'Setting up',forBusiness:!0,intro:'Stripe is the payment company FIG uses. It checks who you are and sends your takeout money to your bank. You can build your page, menu and deals first. Connecting is needed only to publish.',boxTitle:'How it works',bullets:['Until you connect, your page, menu and deals are saved as drafts. Only your team can see them.','Tap Connect Stripe on Home. Stripe asks for your ID, your business details and a bank account. It takes about 5 minutes.','When you come back, FIG checks with Stripe, then asks if you want to publish your page, menu and deals, or turn on takeout.','FIG never sees your ID or your bank number. Stripe keeps them.'],outro:'Connecting is the only check FIG asks for, and it is also what lets you take takeout orders later. If Stripe ever pauses your account, what you published stays up, and Home tells you what Stripe needs.'},{id:'biz-deal',question:'How do I post a deal?',topic:'Deals',forBusiness:!0,intro:'Open Deals and tap New deal. Pick the dishes, the offer and when it runs. Start from Ideas from your menu if you want a ready-made one.',boxTitle:'Your choices',bullets:['The offer: 2 for 1, percent off, dollars off, or free with a dish.','When: live now, scheduled days and hours, or a flash deal that ends at a time you pick.','How many times one diner can use it: 1, 2, 3, 5 or 10. A deal used once has one code, scanned once.','Wait between uses: none, 15, 30, 60 or 120 minutes. A scan inside the wait is refused, and the screen says how long to come back in.','A daily limit, if you want one.'],outro:'A deal you make before connecting Stripe is saved as a draft and goes live when you publish. A diner can claim a deal once a day. If it can be used more than once, the diner\u2019s code changes after every scan, so a screenshot is just \u201calready used\u201d. Pause or end a deal any time from Deals or Home.'},{id:'biz-scan',question:'How do I scan a code?',topic:'Scanning',forBusiness:!0,intro:'Open the scanner from Home and point the camera at the diner\u2019s QR. If it won\u2019t read, tap Enter code instead and type the 8 characters under the QR. Scanning is always free.',boxTitle:'What each answer means',bullets:['Verified: give the diner the deal. For a deal with several uses it says which use this was.','Already used: that code was scanned before, and it says when. A deal with several uses gives the diner a new code after each scan, so ask them to open their QR again.','Too soon: the deal has a wait between uses. It says how long to come back in.','Not for this restaurant: the diner claimed it somewhere else.','Outside the deal\u2019s hours: the deal is not running right now. Check its days and hours.','Code not found: it is not a FIG code. Check the letters, or ask the diner to open their QR again.','No longer valid: the deal has ended.'],outro:'A takeout order is already paid in the app. Scan its pickup code to hand it over, and do not charge the diner again. Want to see it first? Tap Try a practice scan: nothing is saved.'},{id:'biz-staff',question:'How do I invite staff?',topic:'Your team',forBusiness:!0,intro:'Open Staff and tap Invite. Send the invite to one email address, or make a link or code that stops working after a few days.',boxTitle:'How joining works',bullets:['The person opens the invite and sees \u201cJoin your restaurant as Staff?\u201d They tap Accept or Decline. Nobody joins your team without accepting.','If they have no account, they make a staff account with just a name, email and password (a mobile number is optional), and land on your scanner when they accept.','Staff scan codes and handle takeout orders. Managers can also post deals and edit the menu. Only the owner invites a manager.','Revoke an invite, or remove a person from Staff, any time.'],outro:'An invite sent to one email only works for that email.'},{id:'biz-takeout',question:'How do I turn on takeout and get paid?',topic:'Takeout',forBusiness:!0,intro:'Open Home and tap Turn on takeout. One screen walks you through four steps, and one button does the next one. Takeout is optional: your page, deals and scanning work without it.',boxTitle:'The four steps',bullets:['Connect Stripe: the same step that lets you publish. Your ID and bank details go straight to Stripe. FIG never sees them. Payouts show underneath: ready, or waiting for your bank.','Your HST number: 9 digits, then RT, then 4 digits. It goes on every takeout receipt, and the HST is yours to remit.','Two-step sign-in: a code before money steps, so a stolen password can\u2019t move your money.','The takeout switch. You need a menu to turn it on.'],outro:'Diners pay in the app when they order. Their card is held and charged when you accept, and nothing is charged if you decline. FIG keeps 5% of the food on takeout orders paid in the app, and Stripe\u2019s card fee comes off the same payment. Stripe pays you out to your bank on its own schedule.'},{id:'biz-pause',question:'How do I pause takeout or add prep time?',topic:'Takeout',forBusiness:!0,intro:'Busy? On Home or Takeout orders, tap the Takeout: On chip. Pause new takeout orders for 20 minutes, 40 minutes or until tomorrow.',boxTitle:'Good to know',bullets:['Orders already in stay as they are.','Extra prep time adds minutes (0 to 60) to the pickup time of new orders.','Turn takeout back on from the same place, any time.'],outro:'To stop taking takeout altogether, turn the takeout switch off in your menu.'},{id:'biz-pickup-times',question:'How do pickup times work?',topic:'Takeout',forBusiness:!0,intro:'Diners choose when they collect: as soon as you can (ASAP), in 10 to 60 minutes, or a time they pick on a wheel, up to 24 hours ahead and only while you are open. Every order shows the exact time, with a small tag: ASAP, In 30 min or Scheduled.',boxTitle:'When you accept',bullets:['If the diner picked a time you can make, Accept keeps it: the button says Accept for 7:30 pm, and the diner is told it will be ready around then.','If they want it ASAP, or the time they picked is sooner than you can do now, choose how long it will take: Ready in 15, 20 or 30 min.','Orders for later: start about 10 minutes before pickup. A diner can cancel with a full refund until 20 minutes before pickup, and you are told right away. Each order shows \u201cDiner can cancel until 6:25 pm\u201d, then \u201cLocked in: starts now\u201d.'],outro:'Your ready time and any extra prep time set the earliest pickup a diner can pick.'},{id:'biz-security',question:'Why does FIG ask for a code?',topic:'Sign-in security',forBusiness:!0,intro:'Two-step sign-in adds a code to your password. FIG asks for a fresh code before the steps that move money, so a stolen password isn\u2019t enough.',boxTitle:'When it asks',bullets:['Setting up payouts, turning takeout on and refunding an order.','Closing a location and deleting your account.','You can use an authenticator app or a code by email. Backup codes are there if you lose your phone: save them somewhere safe.','A code you entered in the last 30 minutes counts, so you won\u2019t be asked again straight away.'],outro:'Turn it on in Settings, under Sign-in security. Owners and managers should have it on.'},{id:'claim',question:'How do I claim and use a deal?',topic:'Deals',intro:'Open a restaurant, tap Claim on the deal you want, then Claim deal. It waits on your Deals page for as long as the deal runs.',boxTitle:'At the restaurant',bullets:['Open your Deals page and tap Show QR.','Staff scan your code on the restaurant side of FIG.','Your deal is applied to the bill.'],outro:'Deals are free for you, and there\u2019s no fee per diner for the restaurant.'},{id:'reviews',question:'How do reviews work?',topic:'Reviews',intro:'Only diners whose visit was scanned can review a place, so every review on FIG comes from a real visit.',boxTitle:'Rating a visit',bullets:['After staff scan your code, tap Rate this visit, or open it later from Past visits on your Deals page.','Pick the stars, add a few words or a photo if you like. One review per visit.','Your review shows your first name and last initial. Restaurants can reply in public.'],outro:'Paying FIG never changes, hides or removes a review.'},{id:'takeout',question:'How does takeout work?',topic:'Takeout',intro:'Tap Takeout on a deal that allows it, pick what you want, and collect it when it\u2019s ready. Some restaurants also take takeout at full price: tap Order takeout on their page. FIG doesn\u2019t deliver.',boxTitle:'Good to know',bullets:['Your order page shows each step: accepted, ready, or the restaurant\u2019s reason if they can\u2019t take it, and a note when they\u2019re waiting for you. Open it from your Deals page or Home.','Pick when you collect: as soon as the kitchen can (ASAP), in 10 minutes to an hour, or any time you choose on the wheel, up to 24 hours ahead while the restaurant is open.','Show your pickup code so staff can scan it.','If you can\u2019t make it, let the restaurant know.'],outro:'Deals marked \u201cDine in or takeout\u201d work both ways. The deal is taken off your order, and you can add other dishes to it. Didn\u2019t make it? Two hours after the pickup time the order closes as \u201cNot picked up\u201d. Nothing gets switched off. Tap \u201cI\u2019m here\u201d when you arrive so it never counts as missed.'},{id:'cancel-takeout',question:'Can I cancel a takeout order?',topic:'Takeout',intro:'Yes. Until the restaurant answers, you can always cancel, and you are never charged. After it accepts, you can still cancel for a full refund until 20 minutes before your pickup time.',boxTitle:'How it works',bullets:['Open your order and tap Cancel order. The page shows the last moment, like \u201cFree cancellation until 6:25 pm\u201d.','The restaurant is told straight away, so it can stop or not start.','Your card gets all of it back. Banks can take 5 to 10 business days to show it.'],outro:'From 20 minutes before pickup the kitchen may already be making your food, so cancelling closes and the order can no longer be refunded in the app. Questions? Ask the restaurant at the counter.'},{id:'expired',question:'My claimed deal expired',topic:'Deals',intro:'A claim has no time limit. It expires only when the restaurant ends the deal, or when a flash deal or a dated deal is over. It shows as Expired on your Deals page for a day, then leaves the list.',boxTitle:'What you can do',bullets:['Open the restaurant to see the deals it has on now.','A flash deal shows how long it has left on the deal itself.','If staff couldn\u2019t scan a valid code, report the visit and we\u2019ll look into it.'],outro:'Expired claims never count against you.'},{id:'chat',question:'How does chat work?',topic:'Chats',intro:'Once you claim a deal or order takeout, you can message the restaurant from the deal on your Deals page, or from your order. Chats stay in FIG: phone numbers are never shared, and any typed into a message are hidden.',boxTitle:'Staying safe',bullets:['Long-press a message to remove it for you. Nobody can unsend a message for everyone.','Tap \u22ef in a chat to block the restaurant or report the chat. Restaurants can block too.','The FIG team reads a chat only when it\u2019s reported.'],outro:'In a chat, the restaurant sees your first name and last initial, never your number or email.'}]},1277,[29]);
